                        "id":  "lurelight-bloom",
                        "title":  "Lurelight Bloom",
                        "category":  "Ecology",
                        "summary":  "A bioluminescent deceptive vine imitates treasure, numbs prey, causes hallucinations, and feeds nearby carnivorous plants.",
                        "body":  [
                                     "Pale gold flowers and metallic sweetness lure explorers toward sticky neurotoxic tendrils. Damage releases predator-attracting spores, and prolonged exposure disorients travelers into dangerous terrain.",
                                     "Diluted sap serves as a paralytic hunting agent, while the flowers are prized decorations and tactical lures despite severe harvesting risk."
                                 ],
